          "criterion": "AC-210-01",
          "result": "passed",
          "reference": "The actor-owned WAL connection preserved 200 concurrent committed writes while 50 reads/integrity checks interleaved. Invalid multi-row insertion rolled back fully and a reopened store retained only committed evidence. Retention aggregated raw events into hourly summaries while preserving an unreviewed anomaly; a 12,000-row oversized fixture forced eviction plus VACUUM below the 10 MiB ceiling. SQLite backup produced a separately readable, integrity-ok database with matching event and snapshot counts. Corruption is rejected at open."
        }
      ],
      "discovered_risks": [
        "The system-library module deliberately links Apple SDK libsqlite3 rather than a Homebrew build so the macOS 13 deployment target remains valid.",
        "Hard size-ceiling enforcement may evict the oldest unreviewed anomaly only after normal age-based compaction is insufficient; forced eviction count is surfaced in RetentionReport.",
        "Direct database access remains internal to the app-owned core; MCP must consume a later sanitized service boundary."
      ],
